# Files that strangers run or read on Windows are pinned to CRLF regardless of the cloning
# machine's core.autocrlf. cmd.exe's batch parser seeks by byte offset and mis-handles labels and
# goto/call in a script with bare LF endings; Install HERO.cmd has no labels today, but the next
# edit could add one, and that is not a bug worth leaving for a stranger to find.
*.cmd               text eol=crlf
packaging/*.txt     text eol=crlf
